cation/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9e452578c3d2c86c46c68e6503a2af0f92b6119692e48f2aad45ea88a27190a9","event_uuid":"0cef4d7c-73d7-4a04-9c26-b2c53b7c92b9","position":{"commit_sha":"74ab23c905c0f93c91f45b977321422c7b27c0e8","position":"1787444538968079001-0cef4d7c-73d7-4a04-9c26-b2c53b7c92b9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a48915f3af2d23cb75cddd3028786a1b8a60d80f53b5a0a2e96c91bfbcdb64db","event_uuid":"16b7e9b6-1d4c-4e79-b290-892efa66f081","position":{"commit_sha":"6d5f805ab08bcb71434eae6b83ac4387bae886a9","position":"1787444589761097001-16b7e9b6-1d4c-4e79-b290-892efa66f081"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Resumed after a cancelled session; salvaged the predecessor's uncommitted extraction + fix. TDD RED verified: test_breadcrumb_emitted_live_path_zero_local_comments fails on pre-fix code (breadcrumb list empty). Fix: extracted _snapshot_comment_set/_live_comment_set from _diff_comments and _breadcrumb_target from _build_parent_breadcrumb (behavior-preserving, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0); breadcrumb cluster moved to new parent_breadcrumb.py module (re-exported). Live-search path now fetches comments when a breadcrumb would apply even with zero local comments; client-None/fetch-failure still emit nothing (bug-4292 safety). All 3155 rebar_reconciler unit tests green; lint + mypy clean. Pushed as Gerrit change 2128 (commit 56690adc6e43, Change-Id I4507ddd4b4f3e7f36e4e0de3cd6c192ff19a4d58); awaiting LLM-Review and Verified.","timestamp":1787438181192028001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"EVIDENCE (close): Gerrit change 2128 MERGED into main as 6f0c15a21c4 (rebased from 56690adc6e43; Change-Id I4507ddd4b4f3e7f36e4e0de3cd6c192ff19a4d58) with LLM-Review +1 (rebar review bot), Verified +1 (rebar CI bot), 0 unresolved comments. AC1: test_breadcrumb_emitted_live_path_zero_local_comments + test_append_once_against_live_fetched_set GREEN (RED verified on pre-fix code: breadcrumb list empty). AC2: client-None and fetch-failure tests GREEN (bug-4292 unknown-state safety preserved). AC3: complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0; ruff C901 clean; full rebar_reconciler unit suite 3155 passed; make lint + make typecheck clean. CAUSE ANALYSIS (fix-site vs cause-site): the 'if not local_comments: return []' guard traces via blame -w -C -M to repo genesis b534f47a7f9b (carried from dso_reconciler/outbound_differ.py) where it was correct — nothing to compare, skip the fetch. It became a defect only when S7 (2c66-205d-92e1-4419, commit 105d6f682bd) appended the breadcrumb AFTER that guard without covering the live-search path — flagged as a non-blocking advisory on change 2091 and deferred here. Cause-site = the S7 plan's scope gap, hence close --class=plan_defect --caused-by=2c66-205d-92e1-4419.","timestamp":1787441040420215001}],"created_at":1787386183065308001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bbfa954a-2150-4d96-a871-590288782a16","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2c66-205d-92e1-4419"},{"link_uuid":"d799f9ad-f4d1-4d9b-9618-e870085c2977","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c1a1-5006-cfdf-41b6"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nS7 (2c66-205d-92e1-4419) emits the echo-safe parent-drift breadcrumb from `outbound_comments._diff_comments`, appended after the resolved Jira dedup set is built. In the **snapshot path** (production's primary source — the snapshot carries the `comment` field) this works even when the child has zero local comments. But in the **live-search path** (snapshot lacks the `comment` field), `_diff_comments` early-returns `[]` at the `if not local_comments:` guard (outbound_comments.py ~line 635) BEFORE `_build_parent_breadcrumb` is reached. So a drift-affected child with no local comments — exactly the under-defined-leaf case the breadcrumb targets — gets no breadcrumb in that fallback path.\n\nRaised as a non-blocking advisory on Gerrit change 2091 (S7 LLM review).\n\n## Why deferred from S7\n\nThe narrow safe fix is: in the live-search path, when `not local_comments` but a client IS available and the drift condition may apply, still fetch comments (for the append-once dedup) and emit the breadcrumb. The client-None and fetch-failed returns must stay (bug-4292 safety: never blind-add when Jira comment state is unknown). Implementing this inline adds a branch to `_diff_comments`, which is already at the McCabe complexity ceiling (the S7 implementer used `mutations.extend(...)` specifically to avoid tripping the ratchet). A correct fix therefore needs a behavior-preserving extraction, too large to fold safely into the S7 landing.\n\n## Approach\n\nTwo steps, extraction first (behavior-preserving), then the fix:\n\n1. **Extraction** (`_diff_comments` is at its McCabe ceiling of 15): pull the existing Jira-comment-set resolution cluster out of `_diff_comments` along its existing call-graph seam into two helpers in the same module — `_snapshot_comment_set` (the snapshot-carried path incl. the bug-1f3d truncation-guard re-fetch) and `_live_comment_set` (the bug-4292 live-search path: client-None warning, live fetch, fetch-failure warning; returns `None` = \"comment state unknown, skip all comment mutations\"). Also split the pure drift-precondition + nearest-bound-ancestor walk out of `_build_parent_breadcrumb` into `_breadcrumb_target` (returns the nearest bound ancestor key + skipped-intervening flag, or `None` when no breadcrumb would apply).\n2. **Fix**: in the live-search branch, replace the unconditional `if not local_comments: return []` with: skip the live fetch only when there are no local comments AND `_breadcrumb_target(...)` is `None` (no drift / no bound ancestor — preserves the no-unnecessary-API-call behavior). When the breadcrumb may apply, fetch live comments even with zero local comments so the append-once dedup set is real, then let the existing S7 `_build_parent_breadcrumb` append emit the breadcrumb. Client-None and fetch-failure still return `[]` before the breadcrumb (bug-4292 unknown-state safety: never blind-add).\n\nDefault: no public API or caller changes; every existing caller/test is unchanged (the maps still default to `None` = strict no-op).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py` — the extraction + fix above (every function stays under the complexity ratchet).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/parent_breadcrumb.py` — new sibling module holding the breadcrumb cluster (`PARENT_BREADCRUMB_TAG`, `_breadcrumb_target`, `_build_parent_breadcrumb`), split out along the existing call-graph seam because the fix pushed `outbound_comments.py` toward the 800-line cap; `outbound_comments` re-exports the names so existing import sites keep resolving.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_parent_breadcrumb_live_search.py` — new test module (TDD RED first) pinning the live-search breadcrumb contracts.\n\n## Testing\n\nTDD: the RED test `test_breadcrumb_emitted_live_path_zero_local_comments` (drift-affected bound child, zero local comments, snapshot without `comment` field, fake client returning `[]` → exactly one tagged breadcrumb, exactly one `get_comments` call) fails on current main and goes GREEN with the fix. Failure/edge paths: client-None → `[]`; fetch raises → `[]`; live-fetched set already contains a tagged breadcrumb → append-once suppresses; zero comments + no drift → client never consulted. Existing oracles `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_parent_breadcrumb.py` and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_differ_live_comment_fetch.py` stay green (extraction is behavior-preserving). Verified by `pytest` on those files plus `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` (must report new=0 increased=0).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A drift-affected bound child with zero local comments and an available transport client receives exactly one breadcrumb in the live-search path (snapshot lacks `comment`), append-once against the live-fetched comment set. Checked by `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_parent_breadcrumb_live_search.py` (emitted + append-once tests).\n- [x] The client-None and live-fetch-failure paths still emit no breadcrumb (bug-4292 unknown-state safety preserved). Checked by the client-None and fetch-failure tests in the same module.\n- [x] `_diff_comments` stays under the complexity ratchet (fix via extraction, not a baseline bump). Checked by `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reporting new=0 increased=0 and `ruff check --select C901` clean.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py","reason":"behavior-preserving extraction of the comment-set resolution + breadcrumb-target helpers, then emit the parent-drift breadcrumb in the live-search zero-local-comment path"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/parent_breadcrumb.py","reason":"new sibling module holding the breadcrumb cluster (tag, _breadcrumb_target, _build_parent_breadcrumb), split along the existing call-graph seam for the 800-line cap; re-exported from outbound_comments"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_parent_breadcrumb_live_search.py","reason":"new TDD test module pinning the live-search breadcrumb contracts (emitted, client-None, fetch-failure, append-once, no-wasted-fetch)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","c1a1-5006-cfdf-41b6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"649a5640-511d-4473-a619-6e145b353a5c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9ebb-3114-4d0e-4528","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Parent-drift breadcrumb skipped in live-search path when child has no local comments","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["649a5640-511d-4473-a619-6e145b353a5c","0425be8b-e621-476c-8b2f-8c054f5c454b","8541a716-933b-4d98-b26c-ab96b7cffb67","30f99816-3476-4361-8800-a7333a8f88db","443554ea-c564-4a6d-80be-dbdbdf934d91","ded4ac18-3ec2-4a47-909b-730663456d79","d799f9ad-f4d1-4d9b-9618-e870085c2977","023016b8-4f2b-4a58-999e-329cdba96714","ac0b186c-a800-4236-8fd1-542225ff647d","0cef4d7c-73d7-4a04-9c26-b2c53b7c92b9","16b7e9b6-1d4c-4e79-b290-892efa66f081"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787454373220736001,"uuid":"099d74f4-502f-4839-8c87-7da6caaed698"}